campaignTrail_temp.questions_json = JSON.parse("[{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92001,\"fields\":{\"priority\":1,\"description\":\"You stare out the window into the stormy Tampa sky, mulling over an idea that has been eating away at your soul for years. You look at the state of the country your idols had created, and idiots had destroyed. The national debt, steadily regressing for several decades, has tripled in ten short years thanks to incompetent defense spending. Medicare and social security, institutions which many Americans rely on, are close to bankruptcy, and Congressional misconduct has been put on full display. You’ve voted in every federal election since the moment you turned 21, hoping that someday the person you vote for will make a change, but it never comes. You’re bored of it all, angry even. You feel an itch to do something about it. What will you do?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92002,\"fields\":{\"priority\":2,\"description\":\"Your zealous ad blares across the nation as a political rallying cry. Enticed by your declaration, thousands of people send letters, donations, and other requests to your home. With these donations, you buy another ad, and the cycle repeats, each ad putting another nail in the swamp’s coffin. Media outlets who once would have been repulsed at the sight of you a few months ago now clamor for your presence, to give the man who wants to destroy dark money in politics a platform-it's a funny idea. What will you emphasize as your inaugural messages to the millions at home?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92003,\"fields\":{\"priority\":3,\"description\":\"You sit in your office, the humidity of the room making everything you touch stick. You leaf through your phone memos, until one catches you by total surprise. Ross Perot, one of your heroes, the man you have been following since he busted his employees out of an Iranian Prison 10 years ago, has called you. Immediately, the stickiness of your room fades, your heart pounding at the thought of talking to him. Your mind races at the possibilities as to why he could be calling you, your mouth slightly agape as you stare at the blinking, hardly believing all of it is real. The phone still blinks innocently, will you answer the call?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92004,\"fields\":{\"priority\":4,\"description\":\"After months and months of reading mail from disillusioned Americans, and 14 hours of hard work a day, you stare disappointedly at the midterm results. Only 12 fresh new faces made it to the swamp, draining only a trickle of a sea of corruption. Though a caller tells you the true fruits of your labor lie in voter shifts, which you were able to succeed greatly in, you still can’t help but feel disappointed. However, you get calls from across the country, telling you to continue what you started, and take T.H.R.O to the next cycle. It only now begins to dawn on you that this could turn into something much bigger than you had initially hoped. What are your future plans for T.H.R.O?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92005,\"fields\":{\"priority\":5,\"description\":\"You find yourself in Dallas with a proposition that could change the trajectory of American politics forever; the proposition for T.H.R.O to run a presidential campaign. It had occurred to you a few weeks prior, as a way to get a true leader in the White House if you couldn’t get through to congress. You had thought of Mr. Perot to be a perfect muse, and he has granted you an hour long appointment. You sit down in his office, adorned with artifacts from a version of America about to be left behind. Paintings by Norman Rockwell, original portraits of George Washington, his visage staring at you in silent hope. After some small talk about his art collection, the time comes to ask Mr. Perot. How will you pitch your idea to the businessman?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92006,\"fields\":{\"priority\":6,\"description\":\"After your meeting with Mr. Perot, you head to Kansas City, where hundreds of people await your first major in-person speech since T.H.R.O was fostered. Immediately, you feel the buzz of the crowded room, from die-hard fans of your word, to locals who are just curious. You stare into the crowd as you walk to the podium to thundering applause, deafening the swirling thoughts in your mind. As you begin to speak, the eyes of the room now focus on you, hundreds waiting to see where their movement will take them next.\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92007,\"fields\":{\"priority\":7,\"description\":\"Though T.H.R.O’s success has been greater than any organization of its kind, it is still far from the only organization out there fighting the good fight. So, you have arranged for a convention of sorts to be held in your hometown of Tampa, with Ross agreeing to be the keynote speaker. One thing you have not arranged, however, is the people who will speak before Perot. You have made sure that T.H.R.O is not particularly ideological, but you know it's important to cast the olive branch to a wing of your fellow rebels. To whom will you give the pleasure?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92008,\"fields\":{\"priority\":8,\"description\":\"You talked with Perot for months, constantly begging him at every turn to run for president, and each time, you were flatly rejected. Disheartened, you kept pushing on, never going a solitary day without calling the man. Finally, Ross has decided to go on Larry King Live to give a definitive answer to the public. You stare into the television anxiously, hoping for any flicker of light in a country still in the dark. King begins by conversing about talks of a free trade agreement, then asks the question “Is there any scenario in which you would run for president?”. You, America, and the world wait for Perot’s next words.\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92009,\"fields\":{\"priority\":9,\"description\":\"In a daze, you stumble back to your hotel room, millions of Americans sit in shock at what they just saw, including your wife, who tells you “I can’t believe you did that!”. You try to soothe her, telling her it's not actually going to happen, but moments later an envelope slips through the crack in your door containing five dollars, your first campaign donation. The next morning, your office is flooded with tens of thousands of calls; it begins to dawn on you that this might actually happen. You curse yourself at having ever made the promise, but you made your bed, and it's time to lie in it. How will you begin to organize your campaign?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92010,\"fields\":{\"priority\":10,\"description\":\"The glimmer and finish of the Bush Administration has begun to wane, as the spotlights darken on him, they now blaze on you. The outlets who once would have scoffed at the thought of you now stand feverishly in line waiting for the hot new thing to speak his mind on their network. New polls have you at 20%, a mark reached by very few third party candidates, without moving a finger. The weight of it lands on you as you begin your first major media circuit of the campaign. How will you present your vision to the people who made this possible?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92011,\"fields\":{\"priority\":11,\"description\":\"You look blankly at the interviewer, asking you more of the same questions you have been answering for multiple months at this point. You go on so many TV stations that you forget which one you're on. C-SPAN? CNN? NBC? You can’t even tell anymore, it's all the same, and it's making you bored fast. Finally, the reporter asks you an interesting question about the type of person you would want as your running mate. With all the chaotic motions of you and your campaign, it's something you haven’t actually stopped to consider. You picked James Stockdale as a placeholder, and obviously he isn’t staying. The interviewer awaits your response…\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92012,\"fields\":{\"priority\":12,\"description\":\"Your quasi-campaign has finally reached its first wave; a damning story by the Wall Street Journal hurdles towards your ship that details an event where you attempted to find a prisoner to confess that he flew George Bush out of Europe following secret dealings with Iranian officials to delay the release of the hostages, a scandal that would completely destroy any credibility he has with the public. In any sane world, this breakthrough would have helped you, but thanks to Bush’s elitist friends, they have been able to turn the tide against you. How will you respond to your first ever political scandal?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92013,\"fields\":{\"priority\":13,\"description\":\"The City of Angels quickly becomes the City of Pandemonium. Stores are shattered, looted, neighborhoods are destroyed, all in the name of justice for one of their fellow countrymen that was unfairly beaten by their oppressors. In response, Bush sends the National Guard to quell tensions, activity only a dictator could approve of. On TV, he exudes empathy, but on the inside has no regard for any of the people harmed in the worst urban riots in the history of the United States. The people no longer trust their Reaganite overlords who view them as lesser and treat them as such. How will you do better than those bastards?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92014,\"fields\":{\"priority\":14,\"description\":\"It was clear to you the moment Clinton announced his run that he was nothing but a fake, but new stories circulate that seem to swing public opinion towards that conclusion as well. Clinton, during his political career and probably before that, has had a wealth of extramarital affairs, most notably Gennifer Flowers, a woman who he  allegedly had a 12 year affair with. Clinton denounced the claims later on 60 Minutes, smoother than silk, but you believe that America should not forget this unsavory incident. To what extent will you attack Clinton on this, if at all?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92015,\"fields\":{\"priority\":15,\"description\":\"The walls crumble on the Republican Party. A slow decline of the President’s popularity has created the final, most radical brand of a conservative campaign in the form of Pat Buchanan, a demagogue spitting his message to all the far right faithful. Though he never stood a chance in the primary, he took an alarming amount from the president, mounting the largest primary effort against a Republican president since Reagan in ‘76. Though you have been attracting the dying moderate flank of the Republican Party for some time, the insurgent flank, Buchanan especially, also interests you. Will you try to attract the Buchananites to your campaign?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92016,\"fields\":{\"priority\":16,\"description\":\"The polls hit you like a ton of bricks. You see yourself leading in one, then another, then another. You make your fair share of mistakes, dodging questions about your military service, but your zealous supporters don’t seem to care. In the distance, the white whale raises its dorsal above the waves, the glint of the sun reflecting off of it and into your supporters’ eyes. Transfixed at the possibility of catching it, your supporters urge you to move towards it by any means necessary. Jordan and Rollins, in their didactic advisory tone, tell you otherwise, and to “put yourself in a learning posture”. Whom do you serve?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92017,\"fields\":{\"priority\":17,\"description\":\"Every day, Americans see their paycheck get smaller and smaller. Being slowly cut every day by new taxes implemented by a man who promised he wouldn’t ever raise them. Many years ago, they were promised prosperity by the Reaganites. Instead, they have to struggle for every cent they earn, like a modern Indian burned on the cross of the Columbian expedition with vague promises. They cackle from an ivory tower of ignorance at the general public, to the distaste of the party’s founders. Americans now know to never read anyone’s lips again. It's one of the bedrock principles of your supporters that politicians should never lie to the people. How will you proceed in your assault, Mr. Perot?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92018,\"fields\":{\"priority\":18,\"description\":\"The interest in your campaign has reached its zenith. With your name proudly on the ballot in most states thanks to your team blitzing across the country, you get ready to put your campaign truly out there as a real campaign, and not just TV appearances. Once again, Rollins and Jordan ruin the fun, with a proposal to talk to minority communities to try to undercut Clinton’s appeal to them. You know you don’t need them to win, but Rollins and Jordan are persistent, begging you to please listen to them for once and do something normal in your campaign. Begrudgingly, you decide to hear them out. They present you with options. Who will you extend your arm to?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92019,\"fields\":{\"priority\":19,\"description\":\"It comes at you all at once. In a moment, a campaign built by the people shatters in an instant. Stories of your controlling persona and your paranoia at the Bush campaign all hit you like a tsunami. You plummet in favorability and in real polling, and your advisors beg you to respond, to put all the rumors to rest. Your entire life you have won, at IBM, at EDS, at just about everything, but now, for the first time, you are the loser. You decline time to defend yourself on CNN, you leave your advisors in the dust. Now that the stories are out, will the movement end here?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92020,\"fields\":{\"priority\":20,\"description\":\"Instead of a grand coronation that was afforded to your opponents in the form of an evening prime-time convention with millions watching, you are forced to announce your running mate during a half-hour time slot on CNN in the middle of the day. Not many eyes are on you, but the ones who do gape in awe at your selection. It wasn’t what they were expecting, but it's perfect to them after a bit of thinking. But for those who don’t want to think, and are still flabbergasted, what will you say to the people to justify your choice as the next Vice President?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92021,\"fields\":{\"priority\":21,\"description\":\"If the Rodney King Riots a few months back were any indicator, crime has been a serious issue that both parties have been discussing for over a decade. Years and years of Republican crime bills seem to have done little, as the homicide rates aren’t getting any lower, and politicians scramble to fix it in any way they can. It's not exactly a stance you are well versed in, nor is it a stance you would ever want to talk about, but what would you do about the massive crime epidemic creeping across the country’s urban areas, Ross?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92022,\"fields\":{\"priority\":22,\"description\":\"America looms over a new era. The fears that dominated the psyches of 3 generations have been all but alleviated. The United States has been crowned the world’s only superpower, a distinction never before achieved by a nation in humanity’s comparatively short history. A new third of the world looks to America to help bring them out of the darkest pits of hell they endured for so long. With this brand new global order, a fragile peace exists that could be destroyed at any moment. You served in the Navy during Korea, and know the importance of the United States abroad, but your supporters yearn for a return to the isolationism that dominated US policy in the early 20th century. A new century, a new millennium approaches. How will the United States define it?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92023,\"fields\":{\"priority\":23,\"description\":\"Smoke billows from the Motor City’s engine, now broken down. The once shining White City, a symbol of American progress, is now painted a sickly shade of gray, and rust creeps across the once mighty factories of the Steel City. The final nails in these cities’ multi-decade long coffin plan to be hammered in with a Reaganite trade policy years, even decades in the making, that both Clinton and Bush support. It makes you sick to watch America’s heartland cry out in a way it never has before. They need saving, but the rest of the country won’t listen. What will you do to bring them back from the brink?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92024,\"fields\":{\"priority\":24,\"description\":\"It's the greatest invention since the wheel, and you know it. You’ve funded it your entire life, investing millions of dollars into its progression, and it has finally gotten off the ground. The World Wide Web, as it has become known, has begun creeping into houses around the world. It has given humanity the ability to seek information without barely lifting a finger. And yet, you seem to be the only one interested in it. While it is now small, it will grow into something far larger, something not even you could comprehend. For once, politicians don’t seem to know its capabilities, allowing you to be able to get ahead of them. How will you introduce the internet?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92025,\"fields\":{\"priority\":25,\"description\":\"Bush just isn’t it anymore. He once seemed as unbeatable as his predecessor, but the stodgy statesman now sinks beneath the polling waves. With his polling decline, and your polling stagnation, it is Clinton who has seized the upper hand. Riding the high of both his bong and his post-convention boost, he seems to have become the fan favorite. You have trained your fire mostly on Bush and the Republicans, but the opportunity to attack Clinton stares you in the face. It's a tough decision, but who will you attack most in the remainder of your campaign?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92026,\"fields\":{\"priority\":26,\"description\":\"It pained you greatly to announce your departure from the race in July. The millions you had let down all hoped for something greater in America, and you betrayed them all. Bush and Clinton both attempted to get your endorsement, giving you free reign to play kingmaker to the next presidential administration, but none of them gave enticing enough arguments. Since your campaign had reached the ballot in all 50 states without you, you reached out to former campaign manager Orson Swindle to poll old supporters on whether to run again. Dropping out and running again had always been part of the plan to avoid the terrible media scrutiny, and you will see if your idea worked. Your phone rings, and you rush to answer.\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92027,\"fields\":{\"priority\":27,\"description\":\"The time has come. Months and months of attacks at Bush and Clinton have all come to a head in the form of an upcoming debate, which the Committee on Presidential Debates have so graciously let you enter. You come in at a disadvantage with your diminutive stature, but you believe that won’t matter. Clinton and Bush have been waiting to pick you apart face to face, and are ready to finally crush this upstart campaign. In what is perhaps the most important moment for your campaign, how will you prepare for a debate with the twin waves born from the same ocean?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92028,\"fields\":{\"priority\":28,\"description\":\"You stare at the massive TV in your Dallas office, watching the Vice Presidential debate that is about to unfold, you see your running mate alongside Al Gore and Dan Quayle. You had coached them in strategy against Gore, but just said that Quayle will destroy himself in a debate. Surprisingly, Quayle seems to be holding his own in his opening statement, while Gore merely offers his usual robotic diatribe of Bill Clinton. The next opening statement falls on your running mate, who has a chance to make an impression that voters will never forget. Your running mate readies the statement, you lean forward in your chair, and wait.\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92029,\"fields\":{\"priority\":29,\"description\":\"November looms over you as you once again attack the airwaves with your anti-establishmentarian rhetoric, desperately begging your supporters to come through in your rapidly declining campaign. The ship has sustained waves, storms, and even vicious creatures attempting to sink it all, but it persists nonetheless. Trying to come up with new ways to get yourself across is difficult, but at this stage, most voters have already made up their minds. But to the few voters who still don’t know which of the three to vote for, how will you make yourself look the best?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":92030,\"fields\":{\"priority\":30,\"description\":\"The campaign draws to its final act, Clinton and Bush both blitz across the country in a final attempt to whip up support in the areas where they need it the most. You see the gleam of the White Whale once again, and this time far closer to you than the horizon. It's within striking distance, ready to be captured and taken away from the seas it has haunted for decades. It calls out to you and your supporters, each one just as hungry as you are to catch it. However, before you can do that, you must choose where to campaign last, if you will campaign at all. What will you do to prepare for harpooning?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93001,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"Instead of a grand coronation that was afforded to your opponents in the form of an evening prime-time convention with millions watching, you are forced to announce your running mate during a half-hour time slot on CNN in the middle of the day. Not many eyes are on you, but the ones who do gape in awe at your selection. It wasn’t what they were expecting, but it's perfect to them after a bit of thinking. But for those who don’t want to think, and are still flabbergasted, what will you say to the people to justify your choice as the next Vice President?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93002,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"Instead of a grand coronation that was afforded to your opponents in the form of an evening prime-time convention with millions watching, you are forced to announce your running mate during a half-hour time slot on CNN in the middle of the day. Not many eyes are on you, but the ones who do gape in awe at your selection. It wasn’t what they were expecting, but it's perfect to them after a bit of thinking. But for those who don’t want to think, and are still flabbergasted, what will you say to the people to justify your choice as the next Vice President?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93003,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"Instead of a grand coronation that was afforded to your opponents in the form of an evening prime-time convention with millions watching, you are forced to announce your running mate during a half-hour time slot on CNN in the middle of the day. Not many eyes are on you, but the ones who do gape in awe at your selection. It wasn’t what they were expecting, but it's perfect to them after a bit of thinking. But for those who don’t want to think, and are still flabbergasted, what will you say to the people to justify your choice as the next Vice President?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93004,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"Instead of a grand coronation that was afforded to your opponents in the form of an evening prime-time convention with millions watching, you are forced to announce your running mate during a half-hour time slot on CNN in the middle of the day. Not many eyes are on you, but the ones who do gape in awe at your selection. It wasn’t what they were expecting, but it's perfect to them after a bit of thinking. But for those who don’t want to think, and are still flabbergasted, what will you say to the people to justify your choice as the next Vice President?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93005,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"Instead of a grand coronation that was afforded to your opponents in the form of an evening prime-time convention with millions watching, you are forced to announce your running mate during a half-hour time slot on CNN in the middle of the day. Not many eyes are on you, but the ones who do gape in awe at your selection. It wasn’t what they were expecting, but it's perfect to them after a bit of thinking. But for those who don’t want to think, and are still flabbergasted, what will you say to the people to justify your choice as the next Vice President?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93006,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"Bush just isn’t it anymore. He once seemed as unbeatable as his predecessor, but the stodgy statesman now sinks beneath the polling waves. With his polling decline, and your polling stagnation, it is Clinton who has seized the upper hand. Riding the high of both his bong and his post-convention boost, he seems to have become the fan favorite. You have trained your fire mostly on Bush and the Republicans, but the opportunity to attack Clinton stares you in the face. It's a tough decision, but who will you attack most in the remainder of your campaign?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93007,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"It all comes crashing down at once. The MLB Players Union, fed up with the current league management with regards to the salary cap, has gone on strike against the owners of their respective clubs. Immediately, fingers are pointed at Ueberroth, who they claim fostered the need for a lockout due to his collusion with owners to keep salaries down in the 1980s. It's a sticky situation for both you and Ueberroth, you now have to deal with the fallout of one of America’s greatest institutions. How will you mitigate this newfound crisis?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93008,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"Deep down, you knew this wasn’t going to last forever. Just a few hours ago, in a display of blatant overconfidence, Steve Jobs promised to land someone on Mars by the end of eight years under your administration. Admittedly, it's a wacky proposal, one that is never talked about in political circles. You’ve been trying to define yourself as a candidate for so long, and Steve’s consistent out of this world thinking has made you struggle to make a case that your campaign is serious. It has quickly become a headache. How do you talk Steve down?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93009,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"Day after day, it's a battle. Though Lee was initially happy to accept the position of running mate, he has become increasingly bitter. His rhetoric has raised tens of thousands of midwestern voters who had never even given voting a second thought before you. He sits you down in his spacious office to talk to you, giving you an ultimatum: Either give him an established role in your administration or he’s out. It's a heavy-handed decision to make, but nothing would make you happier than working with him as a team. What will be your response?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93010,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"Jeane just can’t catch a break. Every week, a new ad by Bush hits the waves of her incompetent foreign policy handling during the Reagan administration, blaming her as the sole reason for the Iran-Contra scandal; an attack so sly and hypocritical you swear Lee Atwater ghostwrote it. What’s more is her past as a Socialist Party member in the 1940s, something both Bush and Clinton have torn her to shreds over, igniting fears of socialism in the same White House that just a year ago had seemingly destroyed it. How will you cure your new migraine of a scandal?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93011,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"You rub the bridge of your nose in disgust. Jerry Brown, the ideological loose cannon that he often is, made an unscrupulous statement at a rally today, seemingly praising Joseph Stalin by calling him “A strong [...] decisive leader”. Even if it was taken out of context, the public laughs their hardest, wondering what kind of a campaign you are trying to run. By far the largest hurdle you have faced in your campaign, you pace your office intensely, your mind pounding with different ways to respond to this. This isn’t something you can just deny, you need something more than that.\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93012,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"Turns out the college boy is himself a dumbass. Not heeding the warnings of his past campaigns, Silber has made a variety of wild statements to the press, most notably in an interview where he said that Bill Clinton was “Probably [...] a rapist and a pedophile”. Obviously, these accusations are probably true, but Silber saying the hard part out loud has disgusted many voters. Clinton’s done the usual passionate defense of himself, but it's time for you to take accountability for this fiasco. How could you possibly defend this?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93013,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"The time has come. Months and months of attacks at Bush and Clinton have all come to a head in the form of an upcoming debate, which the Committee on Presidential Debates have so graciously let you enter. You come in at a disadvantage with your diminutive stature, but you believe that won’t matter. Clinton and Bush have been waiting to pick you apart face to face, and are ready to finally crush this upstart campaign. In what is perhaps the most important moment for your campaign, how will you prepare for a debate with the twin waves born from the same ocean?\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93014,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"You stare at the massive TV in your Dallas office, watching the Vice Presidential debate that is about to unfold, you see your running mate alongside Al Gore and Dan Quayle. You had coached them in strategy against Gore, but just said that Quayle will destroy himself in a debate. Surprisingly, Quayle seems to be holding his own in his opening statement, while Gore merely offers his usual robotic diatribe of Bill Clinton. The next opening statement falls on your running mate, who has a chance to make an impression that voters will never forget. Your running mate readies the statement, you lean forward in your chair, and wait.\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93015,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"You stare at the massive TV in your Dallas office, watching the Vice Presidential debate that is about to unfold, you see your running mate alongside Al Gore and Dan Quayle. You had coached them in strategy against Gore, but just said that Quayle will destroy himself in a debate. Surprisingly, Quayle seems to be holding his own in his opening statement, while Gore merely offers his usual robotic diatribe of Bill Clinton. The next opening statement falls on your running mate, who has a chance to make an impression that voters will never forget. Your running mate readies the statement, you lean forward in your chair, and wait.\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93016,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"You stare at the massive TV in your Dallas office, watching the Vice Presidential debate that is about to unfold, you see your running mate alongside Al Gore and Dan Quayle. You had coached them in strategy against Gore, but just said that Quayle will destroy himself in a debate. Surprisingly, Quayle seems to be holding his own in his opening statement, while Gore merely offers his usual robotic diatribe of Bill Clinton. The next opening statement falls on your running mate, who has a chance to make an impression that voters will never forget. Your running mate readies the statement, you lean forward in your chair, and wait.\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93017,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"You stare at the massive TV in your Dallas office, watching the Vice Presidential debate that is about to unfold, you see your running mate alongside Al Gore and Dan Quayle. You had coached them in strategy against Gore, but just said that Quayle will destroy himself in a debate. Surprisingly, Quayle seems to be holding his own in his opening statement, while Gore merely offers his usual robotic diatribe of Bill Clinton. The next opening statement falls on your running mate, who has a chance to make an impression that voters will never forget. Your running mate readies the statement, you lean forward in your chair, and wait.\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93018,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"You stare at the massive TV in your Dallas office, watching the Vice Presidential debate that is about to unfold, you see your running mate alongside Al Gore and Dan Quayle. You had coached them in strategy against Gore, but just said that Quayle will destroy himself in a debate. Surprisingly, Quayle seems to be holding his own in his opening statement, while Gore merely offers his usual robotic diatribe of Bill Clinton. The next opening statement falls on your running mate, who has a chance to make an impression that voters will never forget. Your running mate readies the statement, you lean forward in your chair, and wait.\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93019,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"You stare at the massive TV in your Dallas office, watching the Vice Presidential debate that is about to unfold, you see your running mate alongside Al Gore and Dan Quayle. You had coached them in strategy against Gore, but just said that Quayle will destroy himself in a debate. Surprisingly, Quayle seems to be holding his own in his opening statement, while Gore merely offers his usual robotic diatribe of Bill Clinton. The next opening statement falls on your running mate, who has a chance to make an impression that voters will never forget. Your running mate readies the statement, you lean forward in your chair, and wait.\",\"likelihood\":1.0}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.question\",\"pk\":93020,\"fields\":{\"priority\":99,\"description\":\"You talked with Perot for months, constantly begging him at every turn to run for president, and each time, you were flatly rejected. Disheartened, you kept pushing on, never going a solitary day without calling the man. Finally, Ross has decided to go on Larry King Live to give a definitive answer to the public. You stare into the television anxiously, hoping for any flicker of light in a country still in the dark. King begins by conversing about talks of a free trade agreement, then asks the question “Is there any scenario in which you would run for president?”. You, America, and the world wait for Perot’s next words.\",\"likelihood\":1.0}}]");

campaignTrail_temp.answers_json = JSON.parse("[{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940001,\"fields\":{\"question\":92001,\"description\":\"Congress has been the root of all of our problems for as long as I can remember. This isn’t even my future at stake, lord knows I got nothing left to give, I oughta be thinking of my children, my grandchildren, and the millions of Americans yet to be born. I’m, quite frankly, too angry to do nothing, let’s try something out, see how far it goes\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940002,\"fields\":{\"question\":92001,\"description\":\"I’m old, and tired. I’ve accomplished quite a bit over the course of my life, the IARFC and things like that. I had a brief stint in politics, but that doesn’t mean I know anything about it. I’m gonna leave politics be, I got better things to worry about. Surely, someone will come along and think the same thing as me, right?\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940003,\"fields\":{\"question\":92002,\"description\":\"We gotta get these Midwestern Reagan Democrats to see the light and come to the other side. Apparently a guy’s movie-star charisma can get people to follow anything so long as it's got a bow on it. Well, I didn’t come from Tinseltown, but I can still let them know just how much they meant to their beloved president, what he actually thought of them, that’ll get them riled up.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940004,\"fields\":{\"question\":92002,\"description\":\"More than anything, T.H.R.O is a movement of independent minds, not bitter partisanship. I should tell the public about how as long as you believe our system has stopped working, you’ll be a perfect fit for us. I will give them an ultimatum: If you’re tired of the same old politician, join us, we got plenty of room.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940005,\"fields\":{\"question\":92002,\"description\":\"I’m gonna stick to our #1 issue, our economic woes. The people all remember black Monday a few years back, all that “Reaganomics” crap, but the debt and deficit seem to slip people’s minds more often than it should. Once people hear about how bad the debt has gotten, they’ll never want to forget it.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940006,\"fields\":{\"question\":92003,\"description\":\"This is the kind of opportunity that comes around once in a lifetime, and I’d best not blow it. I’ve wanted to speak with Mr. Perot for years, and he could be an extremely influential possible ally to have, he’d be fantastic to help this movement out. I don’t need his money, hell I’ve raised 3 million dollars off the people alone, but it would still be nice to hear what he has to say.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940007,\"fields\":{\"question\":92003,\"description\":\"What is he asking for, does he want to give me money or something? Well, that’s nice and all, and I appreciate his effort, but we don’t need any help from him. I’ll tell him that I’m honored, but I’m not interested, and thank him for taking the time to call me.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940008,\"fields\":{\"question\":92004,\"description\":\"I mean, hell, I like to cover my office in newspaper clippings with us in them, but now, I’m running out of room! I mean, even publications around the world are reporting on us. It would be a damn shame to stop where we’re at. We got a lot of momentum, we’ll get some more full page ads across the country, people love those.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940009,\"fields\":{\"question\":92004,\"description\":\"Listen, we have the infrastructure, we have the outreach, there’s no reason as to why we shouldn’t be continuing this! But we can’t just keep doing the same thing every time. We’ll do some more newspaper ads, sure, but we gotta be giving stump speeches across the country to anyone who will listen. I’ll get the expenditures figured out and get moving.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940010,\"fields\":{\"question\":92004,\"description\":\"Well, why stop here? We have so much potential that is yet to be unlocked, and we should finish what we started. Newspaper ads are fantastic, and I’ll keep doing those, but I think the people ought to hear my voice. I’ll contact every radio station I know and see if I can get on. I’ll do it anytime, anyplace, anywhere. Hell, see if we can get on local TV, too, any exposure is good exposure, I’ll take what I can get.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940011,\"fields\":{\"question\":92005,\"description\":\"Ross is an enigma, frankly. I know he won’t give a straight answer right off the bat like that. The alternative sale is the way to go here. I’ll ask him who he would want to be his running mate if he were to run for president. I’ll be able to gauge his true interest that way, and make my own conclusion on whether he wants to run.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940012,\"fields\":{\"question\":92005,\"description\":\"Let’s not beat around the bush here. Ross is a busy man, and so am I, so I’ll lay it all out on him. I want him to run for president of the United States. We are slowly marching toward a path of fiscal and moral disaster, we cannot be bystanders in this situation. I’ll make it seem like he’s a citizen stepping up for what is right, and not your average politician.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940013,\"fields\":{\"question\":92005,\"description\":\"I’m gonna slowly reel him in, as I’m sure many of his associates have done in the past. I’ll have him look at the people who have served the position. Washington, Jefferson, Lincoln, FDR, Perot will surely want to run at the prospect of achieving a similar greatness to them.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940014,\"fields\":{\"question\":92006,\"description\":\"First of all, I’d like to thank all of you for coming. I could not have imagined such a large gathering like this when I created T.H.R.O! Through your diligence to this country, you have done your duty in protecting American democracy. I would also like to make a major announcement….\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940015,\"fields\":{\"question\":92006,\"description\":\"You know, a lot of people didn’t believe in T.H.R.O when I first announced it, they didn’t believe that any ordinary guy could actually make a change in Washington. I see everyone in this crowd tonight, and I think it is safe to say that they were wrong! Without you all, T.H.R.O would never have seen this kind of success, and I thank you all tremendously for it. However, let me say this….\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940016,\"fields\":{\"question\":92006,\"description\":\"My friends, we all know why we are gathered here tonight. It is because we believe that our system has failed. And that we, the people, deserve better than to be treated this way by our many politicians. Our country was built by people just like you and me, not these modern politicians and especially our current president. It is because of this that I would like to declare….\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940017,\"fields\":{\"question\":92007,\"description\":\"Y’know, I think it would be a fantastic idea to have some of these hot new conservatives on the scene speak at our event. I don’t agree with ‘em all, but it's important that we cast a big tent, and that starts with turning the conservatives to our side. Who’s that General guy, Ollie North? He’ll do just fine\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940018,\"fields\":{\"question\":92007,\"description\":\"Our country’s founding principles that lie in the Constitution ultimately go back to libertarianism, and that is exactly what I am trying to restore with T.H.R.O. Libertarians may be a little wacky these days, but we should invite that congressman, Paul, to speak, along with a couple other guys I know who would be perfect for this. Ross will love it, I’m sure.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940019,\"fields\":{\"question\":92007,\"description\":\"If we are looking to cast the biggest net, then I think we need to appeal to the center. I mean, it’d be great to get someone higher up to speak, but I think John B. Anderson is the best choice here. He shouldn’t be up to too much these days, and he’d be a broadly unifying figure to help lay the red carpet for Perot’s speech. Call him up, see if he can make it.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940020,\"fields\":{\"question\":92007,\"description\":\"Some of the most neglected folk on the political spectrum for decades have been our rural progressives. They haven’t had a true champion since the days of the New Deal for crying out loud! I think they’d love to come out and speak, wouldn’t they? I know one of those new faces in congress, that independent guy from Vermont, let’s get him.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940021,\"fields\":{\"question\":92008,\"description\":\"Come on, Ross…\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940022,\"fields\":{\"question\":92009,\"description\":\"Well, first of all, get me a new telephone line! My answering machine is gonna be broken by the end of the month if it keeps ringing like this! Let’s streamline it into one campaign phone number, allowing people to call to see how they can help out. I sure as hell ain’t answering all these questions, so we’ll get some people to start answering.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940023,\"fields\":{\"question\":92009,\"description\":\"Fuck, we’re really doing this. I wish I did, but I don’t really know the first thing about how politics or campaigns work, and I can’t do this thing myself, that much is clear. We need consultants, lots of them. I want everyone from here to Timbuktu interviewed, I’ll even settle for Lee Atwater’s corpse, anyone is welcome.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940024,\"fields\":{\"question\":92009,\"description\":\"Well, I guess we gotta get on as many damn state ballots as we can. I’ll even personally fund the whole thing, but I bet a lot of my employees over at Perot Systems would be happy to help out. I’ll pair them with Jack, who knows a lot of this kind of stuff, if they want me out there, they have to earn it!\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940025,\"fields\":{\"question\":92009,\"description\":\"We can’t let these people down, but I still don’t want to do this. I remember some of those guys from Texas, Tom Luce and the like. He owes me for my bailout of his campaign debts a couple years back. Get him to launch a committee exploring options for my candidacy, we need to be as coy as possible.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940026,\"fields\":{\"question\":92010,\"description\":\"President Bush is getting us too involved overseas. He just started a war in Kuwait for next to no reason, putting innocent and American lives at risk, and let’s not forget his operation in Panama either. We were recently crowned as the world’s only global superpower, and we cannot be acting like warlords when tens of millions everywhere are still picking up the pieces from the Cold War.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940027,\"fields\":{\"question\":92010,\"description\":\"I remember back in the day I could walk right into Lyndon B. Johnson’s senate office without an appointment! I’ll tell you something: they don’t make politicians like that anymore. They are so far removed from the people’s interests that they can’t even do their job properly. When I’m in office I’ll make sure everyone’s voice is heard, no matter who you are.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940028,\"fields\":{\"question\":92010,\"description\":\"Listen here, and listen good. What we got in Washington right now is major irresponsibility for their actions. The past 12 years we’ve racked up the debt like we don’t have to pay for it, acting like it won’t bite our children and grandchildren in the ass. We either balance the budget or let this “voodoo economics” lie blow up in your face, the choice is yours.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940029,\"fields\":{\"question\":92010,\"description\":\"To all of those people out there who have been cheated by politicians with empty promises and corruption through dark money, I’ll let you know that I can’t be bought by any of these hired guns that President Bush has around him. I got enough money, and it’ll pay for my campaign just fine. You gotta be sick in the head to want to be a politician these days, so vote for the guy who isn’t sick in the head.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940030,\"fields\":{\"question\":92011,\"description\":\"Look, I want an outsider, just like me, to be my running mate. If I picked a real politician or someone well-established it’d make me look like quite the hypocrite wouldn’t it? This movement is built on the apathy of the establishment, and I’ll make sure to have that point emphasized by my running mate.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940031,\"fields\":{\"question\":92011,\"description\":\"Running the country is just like running a business, after all, and it's only prudent that I get some really smart businesspeople to help me out. Obviously, I can’t do this thing alone, so like any businessman, I’ll get a board of other people who know more than I do about business to help me out, and that starts with getting a business-oriented Vice President.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940032,\"fields\":{\"question\":92011,\"description\":\"Well, let’s face it, politics ain’t exactly my forté, and I’m gonna need a helping hand to guide me through the most important job in the world. I don’t want my Vice President to sit around all day and play golf, he’s gonna be just as involved as anyone else in my administration, he’ll be doing almost as much as I’ll be doing. I do need a politician, but none of those Washington Insiders, I need someone more real than that.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940033,\"fields\":{\"question\":92012,\"description\":\"The Bush campaign is accusing me of dirty tricks?! Ha, well, that’s rich, coming from the guy who embarrassed Dukakis out of politics 4 years ago with all kinds of dark magic. Obviously, Dukakis couldn’t talk about this, he didn’t have the guts, but I think I’ll be able to do it. I’ll put on the most stern voice I can and put this all to bed.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940034,\"fields\":{\"question\":92012,\"description\":\"Look, we can’t be ignoring this whole thing, but we sure as hell can deny these rumors. Get me on NBC tomorrow and I’ll calmly put this issue away, all it was was a surgical check on his credibility, nothin’ more than that, and I would never do a deliberate “October Surprise” on anyone.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940035,\"fields\":{\"question\":92012,\"description\":\"This isn’t a coincidence, this is a Deep State plot to take me down! I always knew that Bush was out to get me, ever since I was meeting with him when he was Vice President. We gotta let the people know that this will be far from the only time you’ll see the Bush Deep State attacking me, just so that we can amplify the anti-duopoly message we’ve been pushing.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940036,\"fields\":{\"question\":92012,\"description\":\"Do we seriously need to pay any mind to this? I don’t have the time to respond to every single little critique of me, that’s what the politicians I’m fighting against do. The people that hear this won’t be voting for me, anyway, and this should resolve on its own. Business as usual, don’t change anything\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940037,\"fields\":{\"question\":92013,\"description\":\"That footage was abhorrent, and no human being should have to endure such torture anywhere. I don’t usually like to visit places, but get me to Los Angeles, I want to make a speech there to all the people affected. We can’t just have a presidential candidate fake empathy and expect him to get away with it.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940038,\"fields\":{\"question\":92013,\"description\":\"I’ll go to Los Angeles and try to help out in any way that I can, but no cameras. When I was a businessman, I knew a lot of fake people who would do this kind of thing just for the sake of it. Even if this hurts me, it's the right thing to do, and any attempt to publicize this tragedy would be repulsive, in my opinion.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940039,\"fields\":{\"question\":92013,\"description\":\"I really wanna go, I really do, but I just can’t. I’ll take this opportunity mostly to call out President Bush on his extreme law and order stances, and his unwillingness to go for himself and truly see how it affected people. I can’t do that either, but people will forget about that if I’m able to change the imagery of it.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940040,\"fields\":{\"question\":92013,\"description\":\"This whole thing is Bush’s goddamn problem. Why the hell would I do anything other than let him shoot himself in the foot? The country needs me for a lot of things, but this ain’t one of them. Just let me get back to doing what I do best, I don’t need this on my plate.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940041,\"fields\":{\"question\":92014,\"description\":\"Yeah, we’re absolutely gonna push this issue as hard as we can. I mean, a presidential candidate cheating on his wife? If he can cheat on someone he loves, then how do we know he won’t cheat on something he hates, like, I don’t know, the presidency when he gets bored of it? Americans will need a loyal person in office, not another Nixon!\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940042,\"fields\":{\"question\":92014,\"description\":\"I bet we don’t even know half of Bill Clinton’s tower of misdeeds with women. I want Rollins, Jordan, and everyone else to investigate this further. Get as many women as you can who have a story, and then we’ll leak it all to the press. Americans need to know what their future president does behind closed doors to the fullest extent.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940043,\"fields\":{\"question\":92014,\"description\":\"Have you seen Clinton’s polling recently? That hick is just a sideshow compared to what we have between me and the President. We all saw how scandals worked out for Mondale and Dukakis, and he’s gonna end up the same way. Clinton won’t be able to run forever from this, there’s no need for me to do anything, let the media tear him to shreds.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940044,\"fields\":{\"question\":92014,\"description\":\"We can argue about Clinton being a bad person right after we fix the economy. Right now, our government is dead broke and can’t seem to fix anything. I’m not a therapist, I can’t settle personal and emotional issues. If that’s what you’re here for, go somewhere else.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940045,\"fields\":{\"question\":92015,\"description\":\"I think what Buchanan has done against Bush has been monumental. He was a fantastic communications director and staffer, and I want him to be an aide of mine in the future, or perhaps even in my cabinet. Let’s appropriate some more populistic rhetoric in my speeches, that “no new taxes” talk\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940046,\"fields\":{\"question\":92015,\"description\":\"I want him in my cabinet, for sure, but it would be suicide to make any mention of him on the trail. The last thing we need are scandals, and Buchanan’s got dozens of them. We don’t want these cross-burning, Nazi praising folks on my campaign. In no world will it look favorably on me.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940047,\"fields\":{\"question\":92016,\"description\":\"Fuck what Jordan and Rollins say. Television is what wins candidates elections, and it's been evident ever since 1960. Don’t tell them, but I’m gonna fly to all kinds of different TV stations and keep giving straight talk about the debt and the deficit. I don’t want any advice on how to handle my talking points.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940048,\"fields\":{\"question\":92016,\"description\":\"Fine, fine! What the hell do they want? They want me to be on some sort of weekly schedule? Jesus, look. Down in Texas we don’t take that kind of bullshit from anyone, but I’ll hear them out, just this one time. What do they have for me?\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940049,\"fields\":{\"question\":92016,\"description\":\"Come on, guys, this is too much! I ran under the impression that I’d have control over what I do, that I wouldn’t have people like you annoying me all the time. But listen, I’ll tell you what. I gotta get out there a little more and show the public what I’m made of face to face. Does that make you happy, Ed?\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940050,\"fields\":{\"question\":92016,\"description\":\"You guys want me to define myself? Fine. I’ll head down to Texarkana and give a speech about who I truly am. I’ll fully explain my background, and get rid of any mystery surrounding me. I can’t be hypocritical about the truth, I need to be speaking it too.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940051,\"fields\":{\"question\":92017,\"description\":\"Remember the last guy who said he’d raise your taxes in a campaign? Yeah, that didn’t end too well for him, and George Bush should get exactly the same type of treatment. He knows he raised your taxes and swindled more from your earnings, and he doesn’t care, he’s never needed to worry about money. In a Perot White House, I will belong to the people just like I have in this campaign, and give you the amount you deserve.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940052,\"fields\":{\"question\":92017,\"description\":\"These folks work here everyday running towards their goal while their government puts them on a treadmill. And the government just doesn’t care and continues to spend money carelessly. The government I hope to lead will spend money like it is truly our own. We may be the richest country on Earth, but money ain’t infinite.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940053,\"fields\":{\"question\":92017,\"description\":\"You know, we have a lot of people in America who still have no ideas how taxes even work. I’ll be the first to tell you as a businessman that tax codes are complicated, and people exploit all kinds of loopholes to get around it. This is why we need a flat tax. It makes rich people pay more in taxes and it’s stupidly simple to understand,\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940054,\"fields\":{\"question\":92018,\"description\":\"I’m doing this shit on my own terms, and that means picking who I want to reach out to. We’re heading down to Texas with Tom Luce and the other Dallas guys and we’ll do some outreach to the hispanic community. They’ve been hurting for a long time, and have flown under the radar when it comes to the downtrodden. We’ll head down to San Antonio right away and get it done.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940055,\"fields\":{\"question\":92018,\"description\":\"It might seem crazy, a guy like me in New York, but I’ll head up there and talk to the massive Jewish population there. New York’s ballot access laws are a tough nut to crack, but if we can get the Jewish vote locked down, we could make a real push at the entire state if we wanted to. It's got independent roots, and I’m sure we could take it from Clinton.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940056,\"fields\":{\"question\":92018,\"description\":\"Fine Ed, fine! I’ll go speak to the goddamn NAACP. They won’t ever vote for me even if I tried but hey, what the hell, right? I don’t want to do this, at all, but whatever gets you off my ass, Ed, I’ll do it. If this goes wrong, it's gonna be your fault.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940057,\"fields\":{\"question\":92018,\"description\":\"You know what, Ed? Fuck you, seriously. I don’t need them to win. Why focus on them when we can focus on all of these midwestern Reagan Democrats and pro-choice republicans? Those blocs are what are truly scaring the daylights out of Bush and Clinton. If we can just get a hold of them, we’ll be golden, and we won’t have to worry about minority groups.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940058,\"fields\":{\"question\":92019,\"description\":\"God damn it! My kids can’t be media figures, look at Amy Carter, what happened to her! These goddamn rat bastard elites are trying to take me down! Bush wants to infiltrate my own daughter’s wedding! Look, okay, listen. I’m out, I’m not doing this anymore, I see the Democrats have gotten a polling bump because of the convention, we’ll cite that as a reason, along with a plethora of others. I’ll announce it in the morning.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940059,\"fields\":{\"question\":92019,\"description\":\"Stupid, stupid, stupid! Why the hell did I ever do that? Things are looking bad, but we can do this. Get me everywhere you can, I’m gonna defend myself in front of everyone. I’m not dropping out, that’s what a quitter would do, and I wasn’t raised a quitter. I want Rollins and Jordan gone, they can’t help me anymore. Get Luce to go and grab another guy who will listen to me.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940060,\"fields\":{\"question\":92020,\"description\":\"Jeane knows when things are broken, and is smart enough to know better and get that broken thing fixed! She’s done it all with relations to foreign issues and authoritarian regimes. Well, she’ll help me dismantle another authoritarian regime when I am in office, and bring true democracy all around the world.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940061,\"fields\":{\"question\":92021,\"description\":\"When I was a kid in Texarkana, I never had to worry about people getting shot everywhere. Now, just about everyone living in an urban area does. It's not right, it's downright horrible to see anyone at risk like this. I’m not as tough on crime as Reagan, but I do believe we need to take these “cop killer” bullets off the market. Just as our civilians need to be safe, our police need to be safe as well.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940062,\"fields\":{\"question\":92021,\"description\":\"Reagan did funnel crack into low-income neighborhoods, and that is exactly the problem. The fact that people can have fast and easy access to these life-altering drugs is incredibly concerning. Drugs will take years off your life, and won’t help you succeed like I have. I will be launching a new version of the War on Drugs, and finish what was started 20 odd years ago.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940063,\"fields\":{\"question\":92021,\"description\":\"You know, I really don’t give a damn one way or the other if our crime rates are high. No matter what is done about crime, there will always be crime happening anyhow. What we really need to be talking about is how our economy is being destroyed by our government, and how I am the only one who can fix it.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940064,\"fields\":{\"question\":92022,\"description\":\"Well, you know, I’m not really at all qualified to talk about foreign policy, but I’ll tell you this much. For as long as I can remember, I’ve been fearful of a war, and I think anyone who is younger than me can attest to that too. We’ve been in enough wars since I was born to last 100 lifetimes. I can’t possibly let any more Americans die in wars that we have no business fighting in. When I am president, I will tone down our position in the world, and focus on our own internal improvements.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940065,\"fields\":{\"question\":92022,\"description\":\"Well, you know, we still can’t get our asses out of places we said we were out of! We left those POWs in Vietnam to die! It's true! I tried to go back there a few years ago and look for them but they didn’t let me! You guys need to see the facts and figure out for yourself, the government keeps this from people!\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940066,\"fields\":{\"question\":92022,\"description\":\"We gotta face facts here. I disagree with the way the President has handled his foreign policy, particularly in Panama and the middle east, but we can’t just withdraw into ourselves and possibly let some extraterrestrials make communism come back. We need to be cautious and tone down our intervention, but we need to defend human rights whenever they are in jeopardy.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940067,\"fields\":{\"question\":92022,\"description\":\"Listen, folks, I don’t really know the first thing about foreign policy at this present moment. I will have a wonderful team of cabinet members, and they will be ready to help me out and inform me on decisions I should or shouldn’t make. The United States is entering a new era, and I will need to look at all the options.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940068,\"fields\":{\"question\":92023,\"description\":\"These policies are made for the politicians to make more money, simple as that. Think about how much money y’all make these days and compare it to 10 years ago. That’s right, you make less because of this free trade stuff, and I won’t stand for it. Those tax cuts seem nice as a promise, but the government will just hustle you for money in other ways. I’ll make sure to restore every working man’s paycheck by keeping this policy away from us.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940069,\"fields\":{\"question\":92023,\"description\":\"I mean, we just spent 40 years fending off those communist countries, and we succeeded. However, those countries over in Asia like Japan and Korea have been right under our noses taking away all of our revenue and giving it to themselves. We are America, and we cannot just hand our prosperity to other countries like it's no problem. I’m getting us out of this trade deal and restoring American supremacy in commerce.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940070,\"fields\":{\"question\":92024,\"description\":\"Development of the internet will be no harder than going to the moon. We got to the moon in what, 6 years? Well, I want us all to work together with the internet issue too. I want the internet to be government funded and have it available in every school and library in America by the 21st century. That gives us 8 years to do it, we’ll have plenty of time.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940071,\"fields\":{\"question\":92024,\"description\":\"I remember when I was a little kid hearing about the 1939 New York World’s Fair. The big overarching theme for it was “The World of Tomorrow”. Well, the world of tomorrow is just around the corner, and that starts with developing the internet and making it accessible. Imagine a world where everyone is connected no matter how far away they are from something. This is what can be attained if I am elected president.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940072,\"fields\":{\"question\":92024,\"description\":\"You all can take my word for it: I’m not going to worry about the internet right now. The whole thing is still in its infancy, and we can’t coddle it and then let it suffocate to death. I will create a task force that will research the effects of the internet and then we will take it from there towards the end of my term.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940073,\"fields\":{\"question\":92024,\"description\":\"I’ve been talking about our declining economy for about as long as I’ve been campaigning, and the internet is a great way to get us out of this economic slump. With the internet, we’ll open a whole new way of commerce that’s easier to manage than ever. I promise you all, once we get this thing out, you won’t need to worry about our economic woes.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940074,\"fields\":{\"question\":92025,\"description\":\"Clinton is the new target here. He’s got so many skeletons in his closet it might as well be a goddamn cemetery. He’s sleazy, and frankly just Bush with a D next to his name. Think about it, he’s trying to push a moderate platform that might as well be identical to the president. Let’s try and get some of those more liberal guys in the party to come out and maybe repudiate this “New Democrat” bullshit.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940075,\"fields\":{\"question\":92025,\"description\":\"I mean, with George Bush I’m not so sure where the attacks on him end! He’s the most important one for me to attack, he’s the incumbent president of a country in decline. We’ll just keep hitting on the same points that we have been hitting ever since the whole thing got started. Taxes, the economy, and NAFTA. The Holy Trinity, if you will.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940076,\"fields\":{\"question\":92025,\"description\":\"I don’t know why we need to attack any one of the candidates when they are virtually the same. I’ll appropriate some of that rhetoric that Jack used to use in those ads, you know, that “Mad As Hell” stuff? The two party system is a stain on our democracy, and I’ll attack that as a whole, along with our congressional gridlock.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940077,\"fields\":{\"question\":92026,\"description\":\"Yes?\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940078,\"fields\":{\"question\":92027,\"description\":\"Honestly, I’m not even gonna prepare at all. Bush and Clinton are gonna come at me with some scripted bullshit, I’m gonna be speaking straight from the heart, and maybe even throw in a soundbite or three to really make those people at home electrified. Hell, I’ll get going on some more infomercials that I’ll advertise at the debate if they want a fuller answer from me. They won’t know what hit ‘em.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940079,\"fields\":{\"question\":92027,\"description\":\"Remember how Carter ducked the debates because John Anderson was gonna be up there? I have a feeling that Reagan benefitted from being able to debate both Anderson and Carter one on one. I’ll offer the same. I’ll debate Bush first, then Clinton so neither of them will have the other to hide behind.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940080,\"fields\":{\"question\":92027,\"description\":\"Heh, well, I got a plan here. I’ve been doing these infomercials lately and the people love ‘em, you know? I’m gonna debate from home in an infomercial format, and respond to the questions asked by the moderators on TV, with all the same charts and graphs I’ve been using from the start.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940081,\"fields\":{\"question\":92027,\"description\":\"To hell with it all. I’m not debating these two freaks on a rigged stage like that. This debate is a CIA trap to destroy my campaign, probably aided by the Vietcong too. I’m not going within a 100 mile radius of there, I’ll go ahead and just campaign in the Midwest like I’ve been doing for months.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940082,\"fields\":{\"question\":92028,\"description\":\"Please Jerry/Steve/James/Jeane/Johnny/Lee/Pete…\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940083,\"fields\":{\"question\":92029,\"description\":\"Now, have a good hard look at what the Democrats and Republicans are offering, and then compare them side by side. You see, they offer the same thing, just under a different name. I’m the only candidate in this race actually offering a real choice for the people. If you don’t want to vote for politics as usual, your vote should go to me.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940084,\"fields\":{\"question\":92029,\"description\":\"Well, there’s been quite a bit of controversy around my character over the course of this campaign, hasn’t there? I’ll get on TV and wrap everything up in a nice little package for all the voters concerned with my past actions. I’ve defended myself before, and I can sure as hell do it again.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940085,\"fields\":{\"question\":92029,\"description\":\"This NAFTA plan is going to destroy just about every working class American’s home. I said in the debates a couple weeks ago that there will be a giant sucking sound going to Mexico, well, I ain’t lying about that. All that deal will do is make your wages go down and make the rich businessmen of America line their pockets with more money. As a rich businessman myself, I don’t need any more money, and that’s why I can’t let this deal happen.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940086,\"fields\":{\"question\":92029,\"description\":\"I’m not totally sure how much people want a new Cold War. Bush may have “ended” it, but he’s just trying to start a new one over in Asia with China and the Hindus. If you want proof, go ahead and look at the wars he’s started. I certainly don’t want to go to sleep with the threat of a nuclear war, and I’m sure you don’t either.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940087,\"fields\":{\"question\":92030,\"description\":\"I’ve looked at my polling numbers, you know, and I think they’ve been the highest out in New England. They’ve got a lot of older, more Rockefeller Republican types that I think I could appeal to right before the campaign ends. We’ll start in Maine before snaking down to Connecticut and Massachusetts, and then head home.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940088,\"fields\":{\"question\":92030,\"description\":\"The Plains states may not have that many electoral votes, but winning them is still important. I bet I could see half of the registered voting population in some states. Clinton and Bush surely aren’t worrying about those states too much, a perfect place for me to capitalize on voters ripe for my message.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940089,\"fields\":{\"question\":92030,\"description\":\"The Midwest, Michigan and Ohio specifically. They are the ones who have been getting screwed over by the elites and the IRS for the longest amount of time. I’m gonna go to as many cities as I can around there and show them that they finally have a candidate they know they can trust in Washington and won’t stab them in the back.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940090,\"fields\":{\"question\":92030,\"description\":\"I want to beat that bastard Bush in Texas, really embarrass him. We’ll do rallies everywhere from El Paso to Houston and really make a statement. Then, we’ll head down to Tampa and meet up with Jack to do a rally down there. I’ll even lay out plans for Jack to run for congress in the future, he’ll love to be in there, I’m sure.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940091,\"fields\":{\"question\":93001,\"description\":\"Now, now, I know a lot of people don’t know who the hell this guy is. Well, I’ll tell you: Ueberroth is the savior of Major League Baseball and was the architect of one of the best Olympics the world has ever seen. He knows how to deal with annoying people, a type I know I’ll come across in Washington. I couldn’t be happier to have him on, and you’ll know why in due time.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940092,\"fields\":{\"question\":93002,\"description\":\"Johnny Silber is one of the best, most upstanding individuals I’ve ever met. He’s a self-made man, whip smart too, and kinda feels like a reflection of me, you know? He doesn’t take bullshit from anyone, just like me, and has run Boston University better than anyone I know. Did you know he went up against the death penalty in Texas? He’s an amazing person, and the perfect person to have by my side.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940093,\"fields\":{\"question\":93003,\"description\":\"When I started my search for Vice President, I knew I needed a proven hand by my side. Many people I reached out to wouldn’t go for it, but I’m excited that Governor Brown has, he will be my mentor in the Oval Office teaching me everything there is to know so I don’t mess anything up. After all, I don’t want to quit the presidency because I don’t know the ropes.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940094,\"fields\":{\"question\":93004,\"description\":\"Lee and I have talked about doing this for years, and I knew he wanted a spot as my number 2 when I announced my run for the presidency. To the people of the Midwest: We hear you, and we will restore your decaying cities to their former glory. We’ll get your jobs back, and become the industrial giant we know we can be.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940095,\"fields\":{\"question\":93005,\"description\":\"Listen folks, hear me out. Y’all know Steve from his days working on those computers, but the reality is that he’s a very skilled businessman, and isn’t afraid to cut loose ends when it is necessary. He’s young, but he’s a stern face that will help us negotiate, he’s the safest investment I’ve ever made. He’s been out of the spotlight for a while, but he’s ready to come back in, I know it.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940096,\"fields\":{\"question\":93006,\"description\":\"Clinton is the new target here. He’s got so many skeletons in his closet it might as well be a goddamn cemetery. He’s sleazy, and frankly just Bush with a D next to his name. Think about it, he’s trying to push a moderate platform that might as well be identical to the president. Let’s try and get some of those more liberal guys in the party to come out and maybe repudiate this “New Democrat” bullshit.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940097,\"fields\":{\"question\":93006,\"description\":\"I mean, with George Bush I’m not so sure where the attacks on him end! He’s the most important one for me to attack, he’s the incumbent president of a country in decline. We’ll just keep hitting on the same points that we have been hitting ever since the whole thing got started. Taxes, the economy, and NAFTA. The Holy Trinity, if you will.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940098,\"fields\":{\"question\":93006,\"description\":\"I don’t know why we need to attack any one of the candidates when they are virtually the same. I’ll appropriate some of that rhetoric that Jack used to use in those ads, you know, that “Mad As Hell” stuff? The two party system is a stain on our democracy, and I’ll attack that as a whole, along with our congressional gridlock.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940099,\"fields\":{\"question\":93007,\"description\":\"Baseball is as American as Apple Pie, and we can’t let this whole thing blow up in the face of our campaign. Get Pete to go and deny the fact that he had anything to do with this. It was Fay Vincent and the lack of MLB management that led to this, having absolutely nothing to do with what Pete did when he was commissioner.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940100,\"fields\":{\"question\":93007,\"description\":\"Just fucking ignore this shit. Pete is innocent in all of this anyhow, it's a ploy by the Bush family to get me out of this race. If the people want their sports, let’s advertise the next Monday Night Football game like hell. I’ll get in touch with Jerry down in Dallas, and see what he can do with changing up a few things. Maybe he can get the Cowboys on.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940101,\"fields\":{\"question\":93007,\"description\":\"Baseball? Seriously, who gives a shit about baseball in this current political climate? Look, if the people are really concerned about this, they won’t be voting for me, so I don’t really need to address this at all. I’m just gonna keep on truckin’ and let this whole thing blow over.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940102,\"fields\":{\"question\":93008,\"description\":\"Christ, look. If anyone can have a chat with Steve, it's me. I’ve helped him almost every step of the way throughout his career, I’ve invested millions into that company of his. I’m practically his father figure, he never had one when he was growing up. I’ll talk some sense into him so that he’ll sit straight for the media.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940103,\"fields\":{\"question\":93008,\"description\":\"I know for a fact that he wants me to cut him loose. Well, that isn’t happening. We both have a duty to fulfill as presidential candidates, and Steve just can’t walk out on something whenever he feels like it. This ain’t Apple, and he needs to know that. If I’ve learned anything, it's that politics is one dangerous game.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940104,\"fields\":{\"question\":93008,\"description\":\"Get that rascal out of this campaign. He can go back to his computer business while I sit in the Oval Office changing the course of this country’s history. Whatever makes him happy, just get him the hell out of here and away from any speck of this campaign.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940105,\"fields\":{\"question\":93009,\"description\":\"What a moron. I already had a big role planned out for him, and he doesn’t know it. I’ll just explain what I had in mind for him now, he’s gonna have the final say on everything regarding our trade policy. He’ll make Detroit a booming city like it once was, and restore our industrial might.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940106,\"fields\":{\"question\":93009,\"description\":\"Look Lee, if you really want to leave this campaign, just say it. Quite frankly I’m surprised you ever agreed to this in the first place. If you want to go, I’ll let you, and I’ll even offer you a position in my cabinet. You’d rather be Treasury or Labor, wouldn’t you, Lee? It's yours if you want to go.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940107,\"fields\":{\"question\":93009,\"description\":\"This whole alliance thing sounded better in my head honestly. Lee’s a great guy, but once we both get into office this whole thing is just gonna turn into one giant argument like how congress is now. I don’t want to do it, he’s great at netting us voters, but I can’t keep pretending this is gonna work. Let him go back to Chrysler, he’ll be happier there.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940108,\"fields\":{\"question\":93010,\"description\":\"Yeah, I’m gonna be frank: I never liked Jeane, but we can’t be cutting her loose or anything. She’s a smart person, and knows foreign policy better than anyone I know. These Socialism allegations from 45 years ago have no bearing on Jeane today. She’ll get out there and put these rumors to rest, so we can move on from this.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940109,\"fields\":{\"question\":93010,\"description\":\"Bush wants to play dirty even with his conniving little apprentice dead? Fine by me, but don’t expect Bush to get out of this clean. We’re gonna find every little thing that fascist nepo baby has done to this country. He was U.N Ambassador too during the Nixon administration, he probably was the mastermind behind invading Cambodia and genociding Bangladesh! I’ll tell you one thing, Jeane may not be General Ike, but she sure as shit doesn't want innocent people dead.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940110,\"fields\":{\"question\":93010,\"description\":\"Change this whole thing up. We aren’t gonna let Jeane take this abuse any longer. It's cruel, I’m not sure why anybody would want to smear a woman’s name like that. I’m gonna go to Europe, and prove all those people wrong, I’m gonna meet everyone I can and bang out things for the future.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940111,\"fields\":{\"question\":93011,\"description\":\"Shit, shit, uh, well, you know, maybe Jerry wasn’t trying to praise him, you know what I mean? Maybe he was just talking about it in regards to… uh, Reagan? Or something? You know, uh, Reagan’s a dictator, he was strong and decisive too, that’s what he wanted America to be, right? Just, whatever will get the public’s mind off of this monstrosity, go for it.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940112,\"fields\":{\"question\":93011,\"description\":\"Oh no, that’s it. Get that guy out of here. He’s done, I don’t want him within a country mile of my campaign, we’re swapping him out. I don’t care about the ramifications, just any way to distance myself from this is preferable. Get James Stockdale’s sorry ass back on this ticket, and we aren’t looking back.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940113,\"fields\":{\"question\":93011,\"description\":\"Now, let’s give Jerry a chance to make things right. I know he didn’t mean anything by what he said. He’s a great orator, and has done so much for us, and I’m sure he can go and make this fade out from the mainstream. But whatever defense of himself he gives, it better happen soon, we gotta stop the bleeding before we bleed out ourselves.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940114,\"fields\":{\"question\":93012,\"description\":\"Me? Who’s me? Hell no, I’m not defending this, it's gotta be Silber. I don’t care whether or not his accusations are true, you can’t go around and say stuff like that whenever you please. He needs to go and prove his worth on this ticket, and I’ll be making his leash shorter from here on out.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940115,\"fields\":{\"question\":93012,\"description\":\"John ain’t media trained like I am. I don’t want to do this, but I’m gonna go ahead and personally apologize for the whole thing. We don’t want John making another one of those stupid gaffes on the trail again, I’ll make damn sure of it. This is my campaign, not his.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940116,\"fields\":{\"question\":93012,\"description\":\"Why would anyone apologize for speaking the truth? I don’t see any problem with what Dr. Silber has said. Politics is a dirty game, and if Clinton can’t take the heat from me and John, that rascal should go back to whatever hicktown in Arkansas he came from and stay there. We in the United States haven’t got time for weak people like him in office.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940117,\"fields\":{\"question\":93013,\"description\":\"Honestly, I’m not even gonna prepare at all. Bush and Clinton are gonna come at me with some scripted bullshit, I’m gonna be speaking straight from the heart, and maybe even throw in a soundbite or three to really make those people at home electrified. Hell, I’ll get going on some more infomercials that I’ll advertise at the debate if they want a fuller answer from me. They won’t know what hit ‘em.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940118,\"fields\":{\"question\":93013,\"description\":\"Remember how Carter ducked the debates because John Anderson was gonna be up there? I have a feeling that Reagan benefitted from being able to debate both Anderson and Carter one on one. I’ll offer the same. I’ll debate Bush first, then Clinton so neither of them will have the other to hide behind.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940119,\"fields\":{\"question\":93013,\"description\":\"Heh, well, I got a plan here. I’ve been doing these infomercials lately and the people love ‘em, you know? I’m gonna debate from home in an infomercial format, and respond to the questions asked by the moderators on TV, with all the same charts and graphs I’ve been using from the start.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940120,\"fields\":{\"question\":93013,\"description\":\"To hell with it all. I’m not debating these two freaks on a rigged stage like that. This debate is a CIA trap to destroy my campaign, probably aided by the Vietcong too. I’m not going within a 100 mile radius of there, I’ll go ahead and just campaign in the Midwest like I’ve been doing for months.\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940121,\"fields\":{\"question\":93014,\"description\":\"Please Jerry/Steve/James/Jeane/Johnny/Lee/Pete…\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940122,\"fields\":{\"question\":93015,\"description\":\"Please Jerry/Steve/James/Jeane/Johnny/Lee/Pete…\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940123,\"fields\":{\"question\":93016,\"description\":\"Please Jerry/Steve/James/Jeane/Johnny/Lee/Pete…\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940124,\"fields\":{\"question\":93017,\"description\":\"Please Jerry/Steve/James/Jeane/Johnny/Lee/Pete…\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940125,\"fields\":{\"question\":93018,\"description\":\"Please Jerry/Steve/James/Jeane/Johnny/Lee/Pete…\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940126,\"fields\":{\"question\":93019,\"description\":\"Please Jerry/Steve/James/Jeane/Johnny/Lee/Pete…\"}},{\"model\":\"campaign_trail.answer\",\"pk\":940127,\"fields\":{\"question\":93020,\"description\":\"Come on, Ross…\"}}]");

